# Everything listed here is excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The context is the box of files handed to the Docker daemon before a build
# starts. Without this file that box would include your virtualenv, your git
# history, and a 240 KB PDF — all uploaded on every single build, and some of
# it (like .env) baked into the image where anyone who pulls it can read it.

.myenv/
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

.git/
.gitignore

# Secrets never belong in an image. Configuration is injected at RUN time via
# `environment:` in compose, not baked in at BUILD time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.pdf
*.md
!README.md

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/

logs/
